{"id":19400,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/basic-word-order-in-english/","parentId":540,"order":250,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Basic word order in English","seo":{"title":"Basic word order in English - Test-English","description":"Learn how to order the words in an English sentence. Check the grammar rules with a grammar chart and do three English grammar exercises.","image":"/media/uploads/A1_Grammar_word-order.png"},"modified":"2026-02-19T10:03:18","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Fill in the gaps with the correct options.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"712\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct options to complete the sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"713\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Write sentences using the words in the correct position.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"714\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>Basic word order in English: Grammar chart</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-19523\" src=\"/media/uploads/english-word-order.png\" alt=\"Grammar chart illustrating the basic word order in English sentences, placement of adverbs of frequency, and tips to avoid common mistakes.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h3>Subject + verb</h3> <p>In English, we normally need to include the subject in a sentence. The subject goes before the verb.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><em><span><strong>We</strong></span> dance.</em></em></li> <li><em><em><span><strong>She</strong></span> is waiting.</em></em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>it</strong> or <strong>they </strong>as a subject to talk about something that we mentioned before.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I like your guitar. <span><strong>Is</strong></span> nice. <span><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></span></em></li> <li><em>I like your guitar. <span><strong>It</strong></span> is nice.</em> <span><em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></span></li> <li><em>Can you see those trees? <span><strong>Are</strong></span> beautiful. <span><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></span></em></li> <li><em>Can you see those trees? <span><strong>They</strong></span> are beautiful.</em> <span><em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></span></li> </ul> <p>We don’t include the subject in <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/imperative-sit-dont-talk/\">imperative sentences</a>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Sit down, please.</em></li> <li><em>Call me soon.</em></li> </ul> <p>We can put an <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/adverbs-frequency/\">adverb of frequency</a> between the subject and the verb. BUT adverbs of frequency go after the verb when the verb is <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple-forms-of-to-be/\"><strong>be</strong></a>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We <span><strong>often dance</strong></span>.</em></li> <li>BUT: <em>You<span><strong>&nbsp;are always</strong></span> late.</em></li> </ul> <h3>Verb + object</h3> <p>When there is an object in the sentence, we need to put it after the verb. Verb and object are together.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><em>I <span><strong>like </strong><strong>very much </strong><span>pizza</span></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></span></li> <li><span><em>I <strong><span>like pizza</span></strong> very much.</em> <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></span></li> <li><span><em>She <span><strong>plays </strong><strong>every day </strong><span>the guitar</span></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></span></li> <li><span><em>She <span><strong>plays the guitar</strong></span> every day.</em> <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></span></li> </ul> <h3>Place + time</h3> <p>We normally say ‘where’ and ‘when’ something happens in this order.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>She arrives <span><strong>in the morning at the hospital</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>She arrives <span><strong>at the hospital in the morning</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>Will you be <span><strong>at 3 pm </strong><strong>in the office</strong></span>? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>Will you be <span><strong>in the office at 3 pm</strong></span>? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":712,"questions":[{"id":6084,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I didn't like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> last night. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the food very much","very much the food"]}]},{"id":6085,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We arrived <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["home very late","very late home"]}]},{"id":6086,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Teresa speaks <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["very well English","English very well"]}]},{"id":6087,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Please, can you put <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["in the corner that box","that box in the corner"]}]},{"id":6089,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>After the accident, Jim was <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["for a week in hospital","in hospital for a week"]}]},{"id":6088,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["this music a lot","a lot this music"]}]},{"id":6090,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They met <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["after a party at a friend's house","at a friend's house after a party"]}]},{"id":6092,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Tigers approach <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["their victims very slowly","very slowly their victims"]}]},{"id":6093,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I saw <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["at the library Hellen","Hellen at the library"]}]},{"id":6096,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He finished <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["the exam very quickly","very quickly the exam"]}]}]},{"id":713,"questions":[{"id":6091,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I walk _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10364,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>my dog in the park every day</span>"},{"id":10365,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>my dog every day in the park </span>"},{"id":10366,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>every day my dog in the park </span>"}]},{"id":6094,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Lisa took _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":10367,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>her son to the doctor this morning</span>"},{"id":10368,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to the doctor her son this morning<